From cb3befcfaa5ff0e0f90319f41628d581d5b2fd03 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mstampfli <marc.kurt.stampfli@icloud.com>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 17:11:01 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] buffer_cache: preflush native titles' GPU readbacks, waiting
 for downloads in flight

Native titles keep a page Preflushable once the guest has read it, so the
GPU writes there are downloaded at every fence and later reads find the
data in guest memory instead of flushing.

Such a read must not run ahead of the data:
- a GPU write to a Preflushable page arms the page's read trap again, so
  the next read reaches GetFlushArea;
- a read whose data is downloading with a fence waits for that fence on
  the reading thread (wait_downloads, WaitForPendingDownloads);
- a read of writes not committed to a fence yet flushes them, through the
  async read-back path;
- the trap a read consumed is forgotten on every path, so the next GPU
  write arms it again instead of being skipped as still armed.

Read downloads already in flight for an earlier read are waited for as
before (in_flight). EDEN_NX2_PREFLUSH=0 keeps the flush-on-demand path.
